# Codebase store: checked spec

The checkable half of [CODEBASE-STORE.md](CODEBASE-STORE.md), which explains each point, written
in the order of the process (D91): requirements, then the APIs and laws they rest on, then the
tests and theorems. Every requirement names its evidence. `deus add` compiles the
[Laws](#laws) section next to [`deus/codebase.deus`](../../deus/codebase.deus), and
`deus mdl docs/spec/CODEBASE-STORE.mdl` checks that the APIs exist with these types, that every
law and test it names passes, and that each law states what the spec says.

## Extensions

| Term  | URI                     |
| ----- | ----------------------- |
| `req` | `org.dxos.deus.req@1.0` |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |
| `law` | `org.dxos.deus.law@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: the object store
  signatures:
  - Codebase.put : Text -> Sexp -> {IO} Text
  - Codebase.readObject : Text -> Text -> {IO} Option Sexp
  - Codebase.objectPath : Text -> Text -> Text
  - Codebase.dependencies : Sexp -> List Text
  - Codebase.layerOf : Sexp -> Text
  - Codebase.mayDependOn : Text -> List Text
```

```mdl
api A-2: namespace snapshots
  signatures:
  - Codebase.putNamespace : Text -> Map Text Entry -> {IO} Text
  - Codebase.readNamespace : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Map Text Entry
  - Codebase.lookupName : Text -> Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Option Entry
```

```mdl
api A-3: history and branches
  signatures:
  - Codebase.init : Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Unit
  - Codebase.commit : Text -> Map Text Entry -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Codebase.causalToSexp : Causal -> Sexp
  - Codebase.causalFromSexp : Sexp -> Causal
  - Codebase.merge : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} MergeResult
```

## Hashes and object files

```mdl
law L-1: an object is stored under the SHA-256 of its canonical text
  theorem: Codebase.Spec.putNamesByHash
  evidence: test
```

```mdl
req R-1: a file under objects/ is the canonical text and a new line, at objects/<first two>/<hash>
  by: Codebase.Spec.putNamesByHash
```

```mdl
req R-2: builtin hashes (starting with #) are never dependencies
  by: Codebase.Spec.builtinsAreNotDependencies
```

## Namespace snapshots

```mdl
law L-2: a namespace reads back as written, as a whole and name by name
  theorem: Codebase.Spec.namespaceRoundTrip
  statement: (words : List Text) : Codebase.Spec.readsBack (Codebase.Spec.namespaceOf (Codebase.Spec.dotted words)) = true
```

```mdl
law L-3: a snapshot's hash depends only on its names and entries
  theorem: Codebase.Spec.snapshotIgnoresOrder
```

```mdl
req R-3: nodes past 64 items split into parts, and still read back
  by: Codebase.Spec.wideNamespaceRoundTrip
```

```mdl
req R-4: the empty namespace hashes to f126eadc…
  by: Codebase.Spec.emptyNamespaceHash
```

## History nodes and branches

```mdl
law L-4: a history node reads back as written
  theorem: Codebase.Spec.causalRoundTrip
```

```mdl
req R-5: deus init always writes the same first node
  by: Codebase.Spec.initIsAlwaysTheSame
```

```mdl
req R-6: a commit whose snapshot equals its parent's leaves the branch where it was
  by: Codebase.Spec.unchangedCommitWritesNothing
```

## Merge

```mdl
req R-7: a name changed on one side takes that side, a removal included
  by: Codebase.Spec.mergeTakesEachSidesChange | Codebase.Spec.mergeTakesTheirRemoval
```

```mdl
req R-8: a name changed differently on both sides is a conflict, and nothing is written
  by: Codebase.Spec.mergeReportsConflicts
```

```mdl
req R-9: when ours is an ancestor of theirs, the merge fast-forwards
  by: Codebase.Spec.mergeFastForwards
```

```mdl
req R-10: tasks merge field by field; labels and links merge as sets
  gap: task 823f7b83
```

## Layers

```mdl
req R-11: each layer depends only on the layers the table allows
  by: Codebase.Spec.layersFollowTheTable
```

```mdl
req R-12: add and update refuse a batch that crosses layers
  gap: task 823f7b83
```

## Laws

Laws about pure functions are theorems; laws about the store run it in the deterministic
simulation, so they read and write no real files.

```deus
namespace Codebase.Spec

/-- A namespace whose entries are terms named by the hash of their name. -/
def namespaceOf (names : List Text) : Map Text Entry :=
  Map.fromList (List.map (fun n => (n, Entry.term (Text.sha256 n))) names)

/-- Names with dots in every position the tree splits at, from generated words. -/
def dotted (words : List Text) : List Text :=
  List.concatMap (fun w => [w, "A." ++ w, "A.B." ++ w, w ++ ".x", "." ++ w, w ++ "."]) words

/-- Runs a store action in a fresh simulated codebase; a thrown error is `false`. -/
def inStore (body : Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Bool) : Bool :=
  match Sim.run 7 (fun _ =>
    match try (fun _ =>
      Codebase.init "cb"
      body "cb") with
    | Result.ok held => held
    | Result.err _ => false) with
  | (held, _) => held

/-- Whether a snapshot reads back as the namespace it was written from, as a whole and name by name. -/
def readsBack (ns : Map Text Entry) : Bool :=
  inStore (fun dir =>
    let h := Codebase.putNamespace dir ns
    Map.toList (Codebase.readNamespace dir h) == Map.toList ns &&
      List.all (fun pair => Codebase.lookupName dir h (fst pair) == some (snd pair)) (Map.toList ns))

/-- Three hundred names at the root and three hundred under `N`: both nodes split into parts. -/
def wide : List Text :=
  List.concatMap (fun i => ["name" ++ Int.toText i, "N.name" ++ Int.toText i]) (List.range 0 300)

theorem putNamesByHash (t : Text) (u : Text) :
    inStore (fun dir =>
      let form := Sexp.node "x" [Sexp.str t, Sexp.list [Sexp.sym "y", Sexp.str u]]
      let h := Codebase.put dir form
      h == Text.sha256 (Sexp.print form) && IO.readFile (Codebase.objectPath dir h) == some (Sexp.print form ++ "\n")) = true := by test 50

theorem causalRoundTrip (c : Causal) : Codebase.causalFromSexp (Codebase.causalToSexp c) = c := by test 200

theorem namespaceRoundTrip (words : List Text) : readsBack (namespaceOf (dotted words)) = true := by test 30

test wideNamespaceRoundTrip :=
  readsBack (namespaceOf wide) &&
    inStore (fun dir =>
      match Codebase.readObject dir (Codebase.putNamespace dir (namespaceOf wide)) with
      | some (Sexp.list (_ :: Sexp.list [Sexp.sym "part", _] :: _)) => true
      | _ => false)

theorem snapshotIgnoresOrder (words : List Text) :
    inStore (fun dir =>
      Codebase.putNamespace dir (namespaceOf (dotted words)) == Codebase.putNamespace dir (namespaceOf (List.reverse (dotted words)))) = true := by test 30

test emptyNamespaceHash := inStore (fun dir => Codebase.putNamespace dir Map.empty == "f126eadc463e81d2636be4aa0384edbe2aee5690395678593e789ce423bda595")

test initIsAlwaysTheSame :=
  inStore (fun dir =>
    Codebase.readCausal dir (Codebase.headOf dir "main") ==
      Causal.mk "f126eadc463e81d2636be4aa0384edbe2aee5690395678593e789ce423bda595" [] "init" "" "" "")

test unchangedCommitWritesNothing :=
  inStore (fun dir =>
    let first := Codebase.commit dir (namespaceOf ["a", "B.c"]) "one"
    Codebase.commit dir (namespaceOf ["B.c", "a"]) "again" == first)

test layersFollowTheTable :=
  List.map (fun kind => (kind, Codebase.mayDependOn (Codebase.layerOf (Sexp.node kind [])))) ["term", "cycle", "type", "ability", "spec", "test", "theorem", "ns", "causal", "tasks", "task"] ==
    [("term", ["code"]), ("cycle", ["code"]), ("type", ["code"]), ("ability", ["code"]), ("spec", ["spec"]), ("test", ["code", "tests"]), ("theorem", ["code", "proofs"]),
      ("ns", ["code", "tests", "proofs", "history"]), ("causal", ["code", "tests", "proofs", "history"]), ("tasks", ["code", "tests", "proofs", "history"]), ("task", ["code", "tests", "proofs", "history"])]

test builtinsAreNotDependencies :=
  Codebase.dependencies (Sexp.node "term" [Sexp.node "con" [Sexp.str "#Bool", Sexp.int 0], Sexp.node "con" [Sexp.str "abc", Sexp.int 1], Sexp.node "ref" [Sexp.str "def"], Sexp.node "op" [Sexp.str "#IO", Sexp.int 0]]) == ["abc", "def"]

/-- Two branches from one commit: `main` changes `a`, `side` changes `b`; then `side` merges into `main`. -/
def forked (sideChanges : Map Text Entry -> Map Text Entry) (mainChanges : Map Text Entry -> Map Text Entry) (dir : Text) : {IO, Throw Text} (MergeResult, Map Text Entry) :=
  let base := namespaceOf ["a", "b", "c"]
  let root := Codebase.commit dir base "base"
  Codebase.setBranch dir "side" root
  let _ := Codebase.commit dir (mainChanges base) "main"
  IO.writeFile (dir ++ "/HEAD") "side\n"
  let _ := Codebase.commit dir (sideChanges base) "side"
  IO.writeFile (dir ++ "/HEAD") "main\n"
  let result := Codebase.merge dir "side"
  (result, Codebase.current dir)

test mergeTakesEachSidesChange :=
  inStore (fun dir =>
    match forked (fun ns => Map.insert "b" (Entry.term "theirs") ns) (fun ns => Map.insert "a" (Entry.term "ours") ns) dir with
    | (MergeResult.merged _ changed, ns) => changed == ["b"] && Map.lookup "a" ns == some (Entry.term "ours") && Map.lookup "b" ns == some (Entry.term "theirs")
    | _ => false)

test mergeTakesTheirRemoval :=
  inStore (fun dir =>
    match forked (fun ns => Map.remove "c" ns) (fun ns => Map.insert "a" (Entry.term "ours") ns) dir with
    | (MergeResult.merged _ _, ns) => Map.lookup "c" ns == none
    | _ => false)

test mergeReportsConflicts :=
  inStore (fun dir =>
    match forked (fun ns => Map.insert "a" (Entry.term "theirs") ns) (fun ns => Map.insert "a" (Entry.term "ours") ns) dir with
    | (MergeResult.conflicts names, ns) => names == ["a"] && Map.lookup "a" ns == some (Entry.term "ours")
    | _ => false)

test mergeFastForwards :=
  inStore (fun dir =>
    let root := Codebase.commit dir (namespaceOf ["a"]) "base"
    Codebase.setBranch dir "side" root
    IO.writeFile (dir ++ "/HEAD") "side\n"
    let ahead := Codebase.commit dir (namespaceOf ["a", "b"]) "ahead"
    IO.writeFile (dir ++ "/HEAD") "main\n"
    Codebase.merge dir "side" == MergeResult.fastForward ahead && Codebase.headOf dir "main" == ahead)

end Codebase.Spec
```
